{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-csv-lewj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Resource admission drops installed extension type/field registries from validation and revision lookup"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 (filed 2026-10-29, missed by the blind issue watch). admission.ts on current main still calls resolveItemTypeRegistry(settings) without the active workspace extension registrations in both scan() and the revision-lookup path (locateItem type_to_folder), so an installed extension-defined item type becomes a row_invalid admission rejection and revision reads use a narrower schema than the writer. Verified on main 2026-11-02: the one-argument resolver call remains. The bounded-admission feature that delivered PR #213 is closed, so this regression needs its own fix: activate the target workspace extensions (or pass the resolved registry) before scan and revision lookup, and add an admission regression with an extension-defined type and field."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["admission","extensions","gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"c8ae4cb3c8c844d88312ed5f4cdcb4d35eeb44ee719698770de3ba54170171e0","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7e0993a1cba8c333665704de6f123159b3a4f9257fd79b9f6c5cc42c96465abb"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-09T10:27:44.583Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"ci","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Classification and tested revision\nStatic integration finding in PR #213 at `10678a7187146cd09077a48ffed7003535dda16d`, supported by a bounded public-SDK resolver control on `@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28` / Node24.22.1. This is not a claim that the whole native import workflow was independently reproduced.\n\n## Evidence\n[admission.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/blob/10678a7187146cd09077a48ffed7003535dda16d/admission.ts):\n- `scan` calls `resolveItemTypeRegistry(settings)` without the active extension registrations, then treats a row type missing from that registry's `alias_to_type` as invalid.\n- `admissionTargetRevision` likewise uses that incomplete `type_to_folder` for `locateItem`, and reads the document without registered extension field names.\n- `admitCSV` wraps settings consistency, but does not itself activate the requested workspace's extensions.\n\nThe public SDK resolver's second argument defaults to null; it does not implicitly incorporate the active registry. A synthetic control for20 distinct extension-defined types passed80 assertions: `resolveItemTypeRegistry({}, {item_types:[{types:[{name:\"FixtureBridge\",folder:\"fixture-bridges\"}]}]})` includes the type and folder, while the exact one-argument call used here omits both. No real tracker, credentials or provider was used.\n\n## Expected / impact\nAn installed extension-defined type supported by the native SDK should not become a `row_invalid` admission rejection merely because the resource-admission path drops the target workspace registry. Revision lookup must resolve the same types/folders and preserve all registered fields as the actual mutation path. Otherwise legitimate imports into extensible workspaces are refused, and target/history checks can operate with a narrower schema than the writer.\n\nThis follows the feature's verified [canonical record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/blob/10678a7187146cd09077a48ffed7003535dda16d/.agents/pm/features/pm-csv-bounded-admission.toon): reuse SDK schema/status/transaction capabilities rather than adding a dialect/journal. It also preserves the existing public-SDK extensibility contract. Settings-defined custom types are not the same test as installed extension types.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n1. Activate the explicitly selected target workspace through the public SDK and pass its active registrations to type resolution; use the complete registered field set for authoritative document/history reads.\n2. A plain synthetic tracker with a real installed schema extension, a custom type/folder, and opaque string/object fields passes full admission and bounded admitted import without losing fields or history.\n3. Cover default and injected/direct SDK entry points, JSON/TOON tracker formats, and strict unknown-field policy. Wrong workspace registrations must not bleed between calls.\n4. Invalid/unregistered types still refuse; late-invalid-row zero-write behavior, resource bounds and source/settings/revision fences remain unchanged.\n5. No copied per-package registry or business semantics; reuse public core primitives.\n\n## Limits\nThe resolver omission and its direct branch consequences are static evidence; full native admission/apply reproduction, concurrency and recovery remain untested here. No claim of an observed field-loss incident. Existing all-status issues/PRs and the canonical feature were checked before filing."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-09T10:27:44.583Z"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/tags/2"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/tags/1","value":"github_author:unbraind"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/tags/0","value":"gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #214: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/issues/214 · author @unbraind · created 2026-10-29T07:10:50Z · updated 2026-10-29T07:10:50Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Admission omits installed extension type/field registries from validation and revision lookup"}],"before_hash":"c8ae4cb3c8c844d88312ed5f4cdcb4d35eeb44ee719698770de3ba54170171e0","after_hash":"0c8ddd40bc9017e49820ba0dbd9b71da5b82bad0b2684e448f70651b834c1831","item_hash_version":3,"message":"bulk-item-transaction github-import-61c68195da7b763f 10-update-pm-csv-lewj-acb6f5e41aff apply","context":{"item_transaction_step":"bulk-item-transaction github-import-61c68195da7b763f 10-update-pm-csv-lewj-acb6f5e41aff apply"},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"faf476c38c9f2fd09d89031aec31c135453fd6b718b25e91627a2b5f0f3ad8bb"}
